{'passes': [{'description': 'Convert TMTensor ops to loops and Linalg ops.', 'dialect': 'TMTensor', 'name': 'tm-tensor-to-loops', 'type': 'func::FuncOp'}, {'description': 'Bufferize the TMTensor dialect', 'dialect': 'TMTensor', 'name': 'tm-tensor-bufferize', 'type': 'func::FuncOp'}, {'description': 'Convert recognized Torch ops to Std ops', 'dialect': 'torch', 'name': 'convert-torch-to-arith', 'type': 'func::FuncOp'}, {'description': 'Convert recognized Torch ops to SCF ops', 'dialect': 'torch', 'name': 'convert-torch-to-scf', 'type': 'func::FuncOp'}, {'description': "Convert ATen ops to linalg ops. This pass's main responsibility is to bridge the world between ops that safely terminate the program in case of operand shape mismatches (ATen) and ops where such mismatches are undefined behavior (linalg). To model the termination of the program for implementing error guards, we use the `cf.assert` op.", 'dialect': 'torch', 'name': 'convert-torch-to-linalg', 'type': 'func::FuncOp'}, {'description': 'Converts any `Torch` operators that were expressible as `Tensor` dialect operations.', 'dialect': 'torch', 'name': 'convert-torch-to-tensor', 'type': 'func::FuncOp'}, {'description': 'This pass assumes that TOSA ops are responsible for emitting error guards in case of shape mismatches.', 'dialect': 'torch', 'name': 'convert-torch-to-tosa', 'type': 'func::FuncOp'}, {'description': "Convert ATen ops to tmtensor/linalg ops. This pass is similar to the TorchToLinalg pass; the difference is that this pass also makes use of TMTensor Dialect, which the former one doesn't.", 'dialect': 'torch', 'name': 'convert-torch-to-tmtensor', 'type': 'func::FuncOp'}, {'description': 'Convert TorchConversion ops to mlprogram ops.', 'dialect': 'torch', 'name': 'convert-torch-conversion-to-mlprogram', 'type': 'ModuleOp'}, {'description': 'Convert Torch ops to Stablehlo ops.', 'dialect': 'torch', 'name': 'convert-torch-to-stablehlo', 'type': 'func::FuncOp'}, {'description': 'Converts ONNX custom op